From: cita-777 <cita-777@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:58:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] security: harden credential encryption + remove dead
 conductor

- accountCredentialService: dedicated ACCOUNT_CREDENTIAL_SECRET is now the
  only strong setup; AUTH_TOKEN fallback and the built-in default emit a
  loud warning (rate-limited to 1/h). Decrypt falls back to legacy keys so
  adopting a real secret does not brick previously stored passwords.
  (new test: legacy ciphertext stays readable after key adoption)
- remove src/server/proxy-core/conductor/* (dead code: nothing outside its
  own tests imported it; the live retry path is chatSurface + retryPolicy).
  Resurrect from git history when the conductor migration happens.

Verified: vitest accountCredentialService 3/3, proxy-core 113/113 (19 files),
tsc --noEmit error count unchanged vs main (389 pre-existing).
